AB  - This paper explores the adoption of the European Electronic Health Record Exchange Format in the context of the XpanDH project, where institutions undertake exercises around the format to identify their requirements and level of alignment for its potential implementation. Institutions are guided through a methodology that allows for specifying the use cases, current and envisioned data exchange scenarios, and assessing alignment with the elements outlined in the eHealth Network guidelines. The pilot results of this analysis are presented in this paper, as well as the challenges and barriers encountered throughout the conducted analysis. Furthermore, the implications of this adoption for improving patient care, enabling research innovation, and fostering collaboration among stakeholders within the EU and its broader implications for advancing the European Health Data Space objectives are discussed.
