AB  - India’s healthcare system is undergoing rapid digital transformation, with innovations like the Scan and Share system under the Ayushman Bharat Digital Health Mission (ABDM) streamlining patient registration. This study examines the low adoption of the Scan and Share system in Karnataka’s government hospitals, identifying barriers such as limited training, connectivity issues, and low awareness of the Digital Health Incentive Scheme (DHIS). By combining quantitative and qualitative data from 40 hospitals, the study highlights key enablers including targeted training, improved communication, and enhanced DHIS awareness. Addressing these challenges can significantly improve operational efficiency, patient care, and overall system adoption, contributing to a more integrated digital healthcare system in India.
