AB  - The article discusses the most actual reform of the national economy - health care sector transformation. One of the directions of this reform is e-health solutions. Well-known, that today the Government of Ukraine has a strong political will to launch the e-Health system for the benefit of its citizens and the health care institutions. Thus, since 2017 the Ministry of Health of Ukraine has announced the implementation of the e-Health project as its priority. In the article, we discuss that the Ministry seeks to establish a medical data system, which will maintain a pan-Ukrainian registry of patients, doctors and medical institutions, as well as possess data on contractual relations between them. The goals of this reform include achieving maximal informativeness and minimal regulatory burden in order to transform a highly inefficient Ukrainian healthcare system. Rapidly growing local ICT sector and governments' vision for eHealth predict well for the future. In the example of EU countries, we analyze pro et contra of e-health reform and predict the effectiveness of the Ukrainian health care sector transformation in the nearest future.
